<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/"><channel><title>Terminal on @yt.yeasin50</title><link>https://yeasin50.github.io/yt/linux/03_terminal/</link><description>Recent content in Terminal on @yt.yeasin50</description><generator>Hugo -- 0.150.0</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 17 Apr 2026 20:00:00 +0600</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://yeasin50.github.io/yt/linux/03_terminal/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Linux Terminal Basics</title><link>https://yeasin50.github.io/yt/linux/03_terminal/01_terminal_intro/</link><pubDate>Sat, 06 Dec 2025 20:00:00 +0600</pubDate><guid>https://yeasin50.github.io/yt/linux/03_terminal/01_terminal_intro/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Linux terminal commands explained in a simple Bangla-friendly way.&lt;br&gt;
Perfect for beginners coming from Windows or new to Linux Mint / Ubuntu.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style="position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden;"&gt;
&lt;iframe allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share; fullscreen" loading="eager" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/QsWvEIm2qug?autoplay=0&amp;amp;controls=1&amp;amp;end=0&amp;amp;loop=0&amp;amp;mute=0&amp;amp;start=0" style="position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border:0;" title="YouTube video"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id="what-you-will-learn"&gt;What you will learn&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding the Linux terminal (not Windows PowerShell)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Zooming and configuring the terminal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fixing terminal fonts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;ls&lt;/code&gt; → list files and folders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;cd&lt;/code&gt; → navigate directories&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;clear&lt;/code&gt; → clean the terminal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create folders and files&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delete folders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Edit files using &lt;code&gt;nano&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;View file content using &lt;code&gt;cat&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</description></item><item><title>Terminal Useful Tools &amp; Commands</title><link>https://yeasin50.github.io/yt/linux/03_terminal/02_terminal_necessary_commands/</link><pubDate>Tue, 09 Dec 2025 20:00:00 +0600</pubDate><guid>https://yeasin50.github.io/yt/linux/03_terminal/02_terminal_necessary_commands/</guid><description>&lt;div style="position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden;"&gt;
&lt;iframe allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share; fullscreen" loading="eager" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/s76HUc-xTaQ?autoplay=0&amp;amp;controls=1&amp;amp;end=0&amp;amp;loop=0&amp;amp;mute=0&amp;amp;start=0" style="position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border:0;" title="YouTube video"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id="what-you-will-learn"&gt;What you will learn&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Installing useful terminal tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;btop&lt;/code&gt; → system resource monitor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;tree&lt;/code&gt; → view folder structure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;alias&lt;/code&gt; → create shortcut commands&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;update&lt;/code&gt; vs &lt;code&gt;upgrade&lt;/code&gt; (what’s the difference)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;neofetch&lt;/code&gt; → system info in terminal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These tools will help you use the Linux terminal more efficiently in daily work.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Kitty Terminal Configuration</title><link>https://yeasin50.github.io/yt/linux/03_terminal/03_kitty_terminal_config/</link><pubDate>Thu, 11 Dec 2025 20:00:00 +0600</pubDate><guid>https://yeasin50.github.io/yt/linux/03_terminal/03_kitty_terminal_config/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;In this video, we configure &lt;strong&gt;Kitty terminal&lt;/strong&gt; step by step in a simple Bangla-friendly way.&lt;br&gt;
